From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Daniel Winter <danielwinterw@gmail.com>
Date: Sat, 7 Nov 2026 14:21:10 +1100
Subject: [PATCH] models: add Laguna DFlash drafts

Laguna drafters (poolside/Laguna-XS-2.1-DFlash, Laguna-S-2.1-DFlash) read
the target's layer inputs, including layer n_layer: the last layer's
output, which enters the output head. laguna.cpp now publishes each
layer's input and, when the head input is captured, keeps every row
through the last layer and trims afterwards.

The drafts follow Poolside's Laguna decoder contract, marked in the GGUF
as dflash.decoder_arch = laguna:
- each captured target feature is RMS-normed before fc (enc.aux_norm,
  the per-feature weights stacked to [n_embd, n_target_layers]);
- context K/V are projected from each layer's input norm;
- a softplus gate scales the attention output per head or per element
  before the output projection, as in the Laguna target;
- the noise block attends causally (dflash.attention.causal).

convert_hf_to_gguf converts DFlashLagunaForCausalLM checkpoints: it
splits the fused qkv_proj, stacks aux_hidden_norms, writes the sliding
window per layer_types and marks the decoder architecture. The layout
matches Poolside's published laguna-s-2.1-DFlash GGUF.

Tests: a random Laguna fixture publishes a finite, distinct input for
every layer and the head input, and splits of the Laguna contract
fixture keep the draft's target layers 2, 14, 26, 34 and 40 on the
stages that compute them. llama_layer_inp_published reports the head
input as published on the Laguna fixture and not on the Qwen3 contract
fixture, and the Laguna capture then decodes.
